The isothermally converted $\mathrm{C}$ (graphite) to $\mathrm{C}$ (diamond) reduces its volume by $2 \times 10^{-6} \mathrm{~m}^{3} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$.

The pressure at which $\mathrm{C}$ (graphite) is in equilibrium with $\mathrm{C}($ diamond), is given by:
\[
\frac{\Delta_{f} G^{o}[\mathrm{C}(\text { diamond })]}{P} = \frac{\Delta_{f} G^{o}[\mathrm{C}(\text { graphite })]}{P}
\]

